    "body": "> Not applied yet: D1.\r\n> \r\n> D1: No test covers the \"img\" initiator type for fetches from reacting to environment changes or from lazy-load resumption. resource-timing/initiator-type/img.html, img-srcset.html and picture.html only reach the initial fetch in \"update the image data\". Not applied: proposed fix https://github.com/zcorpan/wpt/tree/zcorpan/spec-review/html-13101/d1 (adds img-environment-change.html and img-lazy.html, which pass in Firefox Nightly, Chrome Canary, and Safari TP).\r\n> \r\n> Reviewed commits\r\n\r\nThanks @zcorpan, is this an action for me to do here? I would have guessed adding tests was out of scope of this specific PR as it's restoring the behaviour of https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7510, though adding more test coverage seems good! I can make a MR for a tidied up version of those tests maybe tomorrow evening.\r\n\r\nPart of the background asking here since I have a quite large backlog of issues locally I've been slowly trying to upstream or raise issues for in chunks, so trying to figure out also best way to make it easier on the review side before just full dumping (I can pre-run some checks I might be missing at the moment, for example)\r\n\r\nedit: raised https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65230 ",
